&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;

&lt;head&gt;
&lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;
&lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"&gt;

&lt;title&gt;AEP Identity | AEP Decode&lt;/title&gt;

&lt;style&gt;

body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    background: #f5f7fb;
    color: #172033;
    line-height: 1.6;
}

header {
    background: #101828;
    color: white;
    padding: 20px 8%;
}

header a {
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.container {
    max-width: 950px;
    margin: 40px auto;
    background: white;
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: 10px;
}

h1 {
    color: #2563eb;
}

h2 {
    margin-top: 35px;
    color: #172033;
}

h3 {
    color: #2563eb;
}

.example {
    background: #eef4ff;
    border-left: 4px solid #2563eb;
    padding: 18px;
    margin: 20px 0;
}

.flow {
    background: #f0fdf4;
    border-left: 4px solid #16a34a;
    padding: 18px;
    margin: 20px 0;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.highlight {
    background: #fff7ed;
    border-left: 4px solid #f97316;
    padding: 18px;
    margin: 20px 0;
}

table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 20px 0;
}

th, td {
    border: 1px solid #d0d5dd;
    padding: 12px;
    text-align: left;
}

th {
    background: #eef4ff;
}

code {
    background: #f1f5f9;
    padding: 3px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
}

li {
    margin: 8px 0;
}

&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;

&lt;header&gt;
&lt;a href="../index.html"&gt;AEP Decode&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;

&lt;div class="container"&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;AEP Identity&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Identity is one of the most important concepts in Adobe Experience Platform.
It helps AEP understand that different identifiers can belong to the same
person, device or business entity.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;1. What is an Identity?&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
An identity represents an identifiable person, device, account or other
entity across different systems.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="example"&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Example customer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Customer ID → CUST10001&lt;br&gt;
Email → customer@example.com&lt;br&gt;
Mobile → 9876543210&lt;br&gt;
CRM ID → CRM78901

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
These identifiers may come from different systems, but they can represent
the same customer.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;2. What is an Identity Namespace?&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
An Identity Namespace provides context for an identity value. It tells AEP
what type of identifier the value represents.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Namespace&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Identity Value&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Email&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;customer@example.com&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Phone&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;9876543210&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Customer ID&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CUST10001&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CRM ID&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CRM78901&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Remember:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Identity Value + Identity Namespace = Identity

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;3. Identity Example&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="example"&gt;

Email Namespace&lt;br&gt;
↓&lt;br&gt;
customer@example.com&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Customer ID Namespace&lt;br&gt;
↓&lt;br&gt;
CUST10001&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

CRM ID Namespace&lt;br&gt;
↓&lt;br&gt;
CRM78901

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
AEP can use these identifiers as part of identity resolution when the
appropriate identity relationships are available.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;4. Identity Graph&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The Identity Graph represents relationships between identities.
It can connect identifiers that are associated with the same customer.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="flow"&gt;

Email
&lt;br&gt;↓
Customer
&lt;br&gt;↑
Customer ID
&lt;br&gt;↑
CRM ID
&lt;br&gt;↑
Mobile

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This relationship helps AEP build a more complete understanding of a
customer across different systems.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;5. Tata / Croma Example&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Consider a Tata ecosystem containing Croma, Tata Motors and Tata Insurance.
A customer may interact with multiple Tata businesses using different
identifiers.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="example"&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Customer:&lt;/strong&gt; CUST10001&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Croma → customer@example.com&lt;br&gt;
Tata Motors → CRM78901&lt;br&gt;
Tata Insurance → 9876543210&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Common Customer ID → CUST10001

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="flow"&gt;

Croma
+
Tata Motors
+
Tata Insurance
↓
Identity Resolution
↓
Unified Customer Understanding

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;6. Identity in an XDM Schema&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
An XDM field can be configured to participate in identity handling.
For example, a Customer ID or Email field can be designated as an identity
when the data model and use case require it.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="example"&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Customer ID&lt;br&gt;
Type → String&lt;br&gt;
Identity → Yes&lt;br&gt;
Identity Namespace → Customer ID

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;7. Primary Identity&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
A primary identity can be designated for a record when defining the identity
behavior of the schema.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;

Example:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

Customer ID = CUST10001&lt;br&gt;
Namespace = Customer ID&lt;br&gt;
Primary Identity = Yes

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;8. Identity Resolution&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Identity resolution is the process of determining relationships between
different identity values so that customer information from different
sources can be connected.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="flow"&gt;

Email
+
Mobile
+
CRM ID
+
Customer ID
↓
Identity Resolution
↓
Customer Profile

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;9. Why Identity is Important in AEP&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;

&lt;li&gt;Connects customer information from different systems&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;Supports unified customer profiles&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;Helps connect online and offline interactions&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;Supports customer journey analysis&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;Can support segmentation and activation use cases&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;li&gt;Helps understand relationships between identifiers&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;10. Identity vs Identity Namespace&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;table&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Identity&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Identity Namespace&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The actual identifier value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Defines the type/context of the identifier&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CUST10001&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Customer ID&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;customer@example.com&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Email&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;9876543210&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Phone&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;11. Developer View&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
As an AEP developer, you should understand how identity information moves
from source data into XDM, datasets and ultimately customer profiles.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="flow"&gt;

Source Data
↓
XDM Schema
↓
Identity Field
↓
Identity Namespace
↓
Dataset
↓
Identity Graph
↓
Real-Time Customer Profile

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;12. Interview Questions&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;What is an identity in AEP?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
An identity is an identifier representing a person, device, account or
other entity.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;What is an identity namespace?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
An identity namespace provides context for an identity value, such as Email,
Phone or Customer ID.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;What is an identity graph?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
An identity graph represents relationships between identity values and
helps connect identifiers associated with the same entity.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Why is identity important in AEP?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Identity allows data from different sources and systems to be connected
when those identifiers represent the same customer or entity.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;13. Quick Revision&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Identity&lt;/strong&gt; → Who or what is being identified?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Identity Value&lt;/strong&gt; → The actual identifier&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Identity Namespace&lt;/strong&gt; → What type of identifier is it?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Identity Graph&lt;/strong&gt; → How are identifiers related?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Identity Resolution&lt;/strong&gt; → Connecting related identities

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;/body&gt;

&lt;/html&gt;
